+
+Background Dice helps assess the other side of the foreground boundary.
+A missed foreground voxel is wrongly labelled as background, while an
+extra foreground voxel is wrongly removed from background. Both errors
+affect background Dice: reducing misses can therefore outweigh an
+increase in extra foreground. For the selected objectives, mean
+foreground and background Dice both improve, in the adaptation studies
+and the comparisons from scratch. This does not mean that every kind
+of error decreases.
+
+We also average Dice across all classes, giving equal weight to
+background, anterior and posterior on MSD, or to background and the
+single foreground class on the binary tasks. Background Dice is already
+close to 100\%, and its gains are much smaller than foreground gains.
+Including it therefore raises the absolute class average but reduces
+the size of the improvement (Figure~\ref{fig:metric-sensitivity-key-results}).
 
